  "notes": [
    "Transcribed for Ben to edit. Times are girls' standards only.",
    "Cheshire County 2027 consideration times, age at 31 December 2027, achieved at licensed meets since 1 January 2026. The championships are short course (25m): the 2027 entry forms accept a 25m time or a 50m time converted to 25m. Source PDF: https://results.swimcheshire.org/events/2027/Champs/documents/2027ConsiderationTimes.pdf and meet index https://results.swimcheshire.org/events/2027/champsindex.html. These are consideration times, not a guaranteed selection.",
    "The county PDF prints 5.15..00 for girls 13 years 400m freestyle and 2.49..00 for girls 13 years 200m backstroke (a doubled dot). Both are stored here as 5:15.00 and 2:49.00.",
    "Swim England North West Summer Regionals 2027 (SS27) long course lower-limit qualifying times, age at 31 December 2027, achieved from 4 May 2026 until 31 March 2027 at level 1\u20133 meets. Short course times converted to long course with the Swim England equivalent time algorithm are accepted. Source: https://swimnorthwest.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/SS27_qualifying_times.pdf.",
    "100m IM has a county consideration time and no North West summer qualifying time. The published equivalent-time table has no 100m IM factor, so that event is never converted between courses.",
    "Open county ages are 17 and over. Regional 11 and 12 share one band."
